==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|distingwen}}, from {{der|en|fro|distinguer}}, from {{der|en|la|distinguo|distinguere|to separate, divide, distinguish, set off, adorn, literally mark off}}, from {{m|la|di-}}, {{m|la|dis-||apart}} + {{m|la|stinguo|stinguere}}, related to {{cog|en|stink}}. Compare {{m|en|extinguish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|dĭ-stĭngʹgwĭsh}}, {{IPA|en|/dɪˈstɪŋ.ɡwɪʃ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-distinguish.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪŋɡwɪʃ|s=3}}
* {{hyph|en|dis|tin|guish}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[recognize]] someone or something as [[different]] from others based on its characteristics.
#: {{syn|en|differentiate|discriminate|Thesaurus:tell apart}}
#: {{ant|en|confuse}}
#* {{quote-book|en|author=De Lacy O'Leary|title=[[S:Arabic Thought and Its Place in History|Arabic Thought and Its Place in History]]|year=1922|passage=It had begun to take a leading place even in the days of the Ptolemies, and in scientific, as '''distinguished''' from purely literary work, it had assumed a position of primary importance early in the Christian era.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Calvin D. Linton|title=In Defense of a Liberal Arts Education|magazine=w:Christianity Today|url=https://www.christianitytoday.com/1974/05/in-defense-of-liberal-arts-education/|date=1974-05-24|passage=Morality is that characteristic which '''distinguishes''' human beings from animals, and virtue is, by definition, the unique quality of manliness (manlikeness) (see Eric Partridge’s ''Origins'', 1959, p. 783).|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240920093638/https://www.christianitytoday.com/1974/05/in-defense-of-liberal-arts-education/}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|year=2012
|month=March-April
|author=w:Jeremy Bernstein
|title=A Palette of Particles
|volume=100
|issue=2
|page=146
|magazine=w:American Scientist
|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/a-palette-of-particles
|passage=The physics of elementary particles in the 20th century was '''distinguished''' by the observation of particles whose existence had been predicted by theorists sometimes decades earlier.
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120430204119/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2012/2/a-palette-of-particles}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[see]] someone or something [[clearly]] or [[distinctly]].
#: {{syn|en|discern|make out}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|reflexive}} To make [[noticeably]] different or [[better]] from others through [[accomplishment]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The soldier '''distinguished''' himself in combat and received a medal.}}
#* '''1784''': William Jones, ''The Description and Use of a New Portable Orrery, &c.'', [http://www.google.co.uk/books?id=4SoIAAAAIAAJ&pg=PA1&dq=ph%C3%A6nomena#PPA1,M1 P<small>REFACE</small>]
#*: T<small>HE</small> favourable reception the Orrery has met with from Perſons of the firſt diſtinction, and from Gentlemen and Ladies in general, has induced me to add to it ſeveral new improvements in order to give it a degree of Perfection; and '''diſtinguiſh''' it from others; which by Piracy, or Imitation, may be introduced to the Public.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confer]] an [[honor]] upon.
#: {{ux|en|The soldier was '''distinguished''' with a medal for his bravery.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To make to differ.
#* {{RQ:Douay Challoner Bible|NT|1 Corinthians|4|7|317|For who '''diſtinguiſheth''' thee?|pageref=n325}}

====Usage notes====
* In the sense of ''perceiving a difference,'' the term is less formal than {{m|en|differentiate}} or {{m|en|discriminate}}, but more formal than the colloquial expression ''tell the difference.'' In the sense of {{m|en|stand out|standing out}}, it is less formal than {{m|en|singularize}}.

